# Coding Conventions — Next.js

## Server vs Client Components

```tsx
// ✅ Server Component (default) — no directive needed
export default async function UserPage({ params }) {
  const user = await fetchUser(params.id); // fetch directly, no useEffect needed
  return <UserProfile user={user} />;
}

// ✅ Client Component — only when interactivity is needed
'use client';
export function LikeButton({ postId }) {
  const [liked, setLiked] = useState(false);
  return <button onClick={() => setLiked(true)}>...</button>;
}
```

---

## Server Actions (Data Mutation)

Co-locate actions in the same route segment:

```typescript
// app/settings/actions.ts
'use server';

export async function updateProfile(formData: FormData) {
  // validate, update DB
  revalidatePath('/settings');
  return { success: true };
}
```

- Return `{ error?: string; message?: string }` — do not throw exceptions out
- Use `redirect()` on success if page navigation is needed

---

## Form Pattern

```tsx
// Label ABOVE field, never use placeholder as a label
<label htmlFor="email">Email</label>
<input
  id="email"
  type="email"
  placeholder="name@example.com"    // Helper text, not label
  autoComplete="email"               // REQUIRED for email/password fields
/>
// Error rendered below the field
{error && <p className="text-red-500 text-sm">{error}</p>}
```

---

## Naming Convention

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Component file | PascalCase | `UserProfile.tsx`, `LoginForm.tsx` |
| Route segment folder | kebab-case | `user-settings/`, `blog-posts/` |
| Server Action | camelCase | `updateProfile`, `deletePost` |
| Utility function | camelCase | `formatDate`, `cn` |
| Type / Interface | PascalCase | `UserProfile`, `ApiResponse` |
